# Custom behavioral rule: catches high-rate connection bursts (scans/floods)
# by SYN-packet volume rather than packet content, closing a gap the
# default ET Open signature ruleset doesn't cover (a scan is a behavior
# across many packets, not a fixed single-packet pattern).
#
# Flags any source sending 15+ SYN packets within a 5-second window.
# Verified: 1,903 hits against a live Nmap scan, correct source/destination,
# confirmed flowing end-to-end into Wazuh as signature_id 1000001.
#
# Known limitation (see README "Key Findings"): this counts raw volume only,
# with no destination-port-diversity check, so it can't on its own distinguish
# a real multi-port scan from many connections to one port (e.g. a brute-force,
# or normal bursty traffic to a single service) - see the pass rule below and
# Wazuh rule 60122 for how that gap is closed at other layers.

alert tcp any any -> $HOME_NET any (msg:"CUSTOM Possible port scan detected - high connection rate"; flags:S; detection_filter:track by_src, count 15, seconds 5; sid:1000001; rev:1;)
